From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: phy: qcom-qmp-combo: make the DisplayPort bridge optional

Register the DisplayPort bridge only when a device graph is present.

Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/e8fcf33971263f28085dbc0dbe5039438bf76c13
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index c39ced168d035ef200af301feb7bf45bb764aaaa..8009e29b7eb416133796d2bea29374f34df85f8b 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -5283,9 +5283,12 @@ static int qmp_combo_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = drm_aux_bridge_register(dev);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_node_put;
+	/* USB-only descriptions do not have a downstream display bridge. */
+	if (of_graph_is_present(dev->of_node)) {
+		ret = drm_aux_bridge_register(dev);
+		if (ret)
+			goto err_node_put;
+	}
 
